1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:13,930
<i>The second quest</i>…

2
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,181
THE SECOND QUEST IS REVEALED

3
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:17,434
is Baengnokdam Crater Lake
at Hallasan Mountain.

4
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:19,769
Goodbye!

5
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:21,896
I somewhat expected it, but…

6
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:24,733
THE HIGHEST MOUNTAIN IN KOREA
HALLASAN, 1,950 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

7
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,860
President Tar,
could you brief us on the schedule?

8
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,319
HE PLANNED
FOR THEIR HALLASAN CLIMB

9
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:29,529
I need to see the schedule.

10
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:33,783
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST EXPEDITION
TO JEJU ISLAND

11
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:37,787
GIMPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT
JEJU INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

12
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:41,041
ARRIVAL AT JEJU INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

13
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:43,835
Hey, I'll go withdraw money for the fee…
I mean, the fine.

14
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,464
TAEBAEKSAN

15
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:50,425
DESCEND CLUB RULES
NEGATIVE COMMENT: 300,000-WON FINE

16
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:53,136
I really can't do this show.

17
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:56,097
Jung-won? Jung-won.

18
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:58,641
INCURS 300,000-WON FINE

19
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,769
-Can you do this show?
-Of course.

20
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:02,854
It's 300,000 won, right?

21
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:05,565
MINUS 300,000 WON

22
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:11,196
STRENGTHS: ADMIT MISTAKES
AND ENGAGES IN SELF-REFLECTION FAST

23
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:12,739
First off, I'll pay the fine.

24
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:15,158
-President Tar, here's the fine.
-The fine.

25
00:01:15,658 --> 00:01:17,911
-I should count to make sure, right?
-You should.

26
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:21,081
But the manager manages our money.

27
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:22,957
-Right, give it back.
-Okay.

28
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:24,834
I counted it correctly.

29
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:26,211
President Tar, where to now?

30
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:27,670
-To rent a car.
-Yes.

31
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:30,048
LET'S GO RENT A CAR FIRST

32
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:31,966
DOMESTIC ARRIVALS

33
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:32,926
The weather's okay.

34
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:34,594
The weather's so nice.

35
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,096
JEJU ISLAND
CURRENTLY 6.4°C

36
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,181
The weather's good.

37
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:39,933
I think we could hike in hoodies.

38
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:40,850
Yeah.

39
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:43,102
-We won't need padded jackets.
-Right.

40
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:44,479
Right, we won't.

41
00:01:44,562 --> 00:01:46,064
Doesn't it feel like spring?

42
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:48,858
IT'S FEBRUARY
BUT IT FEELS LIKE SPRING IN JEJU

43
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:50,693
Why is the weather so nice?

44
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:51,653
It's so good.

45
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:52,862
This is insane.

46
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:55,240
THE JEJU EXPEDITION IS OFF TO A GOOD START

47
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:58,034
We can see
the Hallasan summit from here.

48
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,410
-What?
-Where?

49
00:02:00,036 --> 00:02:02,080
We can see it so clearly.

50
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,208
Is that Hallasan?

51
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,876
The air must be really clear.

52
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:14,801
THANKS TO CLEAR WEATHER

53
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:17,053
HALLASAN IS VISIBLE FROM EVERYWHERE

54
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:18,429
Who's going to drive?

55
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:20,932
I'll do it today,
since you did it last time.

56
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:22,100
No, it's all right.

57
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:23,059
Chae-min is driving?

58
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,477
Area C11 is here.

59
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:27,522
LCM AKA LEE CHAE-MIN IS DRIVING TODAY

60
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:30,483
Should we go eat that thing first?

61
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:32,402
-<i>Mulhoe,</i> right?
-Yes.

62
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,611
Here we go.

63
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:37,907
ABALONE RESTAURANT
JEJU INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

64
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:39,659
To avoid confusion this time,

65
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:42,120
I'll pay for everything
and tell you the amount later.

66
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:43,329
Sure, sounds great.

67
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,040
WE ALWAYS SPLIT THE BILL EVENLY

68
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:49,961
Let's try it.

69
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:52,005
-"Abalone restaurant."
-This will be good.

70
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:53,548
Gosh, there are so many good dishes.

71
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:55,300
They're all abalone dishes. Nice.

72
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:56,885
So many delicious dishes.

73
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:58,511
IT HAS EVERY ABALONE DISH

74
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:00,972
-We didn't get to eat abalone in Gangwon.
-Right.

75
00:03:01,055 --> 00:03:03,808
So while looking for restaurants,
I thought we should have it

76
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,643
as soon as we get to Jeju.

77
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,437
Should we just order a full spread?

78
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,354
Sure.

79
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:11,024
WITH ABALONE CAUGHT BY HAENYEO

80
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:14,277
A TABLE FULL OF ABALONE DISHES
TO GIVE THEM ENERGY FOR HIKING

81
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,988
ABALONE MULHOE

82
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:18,740
We should use wooden chopsticks for this.

83
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:19,657
ABALONE SASHIMI

84
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:22,368
GRILLED ABALONE

85
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:24,996
ABALONE STEW

86
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:27,624
ABALONE PORRIDGE

87
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:30,209
OCTOPUS, SEA PINEAPPLE, SEA CUCUMBER
TILEFISH, SEA URCHIN SOUP

88
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:31,586
It's an abalone feast.

89
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:34,130
Gosh, this is amazing.

90
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,341
-Bon appétit.
-Bon appétit.

91
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:37,634
-Thank you for the food.
-Gosh.

92
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:41,804
CHEWY ABALONE SASHIMI FIRST

93
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:43,640
It's good.

94
00:03:46,517 --> 00:03:47,518
DOWOON TRIES MULHOE FIRST

95
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,270
-Thank you for the food.
-Thank you.

96
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:55,818
<i>Mulhoe</i> is so fresh.

97
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:58,321
-The rice has beans too.
-I'll try butter-grilled one.

98
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:04,786
-Is it good?
-It melts in your mouth.

99
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,164
We're practically swimming
in a sea of abalone.

100
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:12,210
SAVORING THE SEA URCHIN AND SEAWEED SOUP

101
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:21,344
-Should we have ordered one more soup?
-No.

102
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,388
-We can just eat a variety of dishes.
-Right.

103
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:24,389
HE WANTS MORE SOUP

104
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:27,016
THEY TRY THE OCTOPUS
AND TURBAN SNAIL SKEWERS TOO

105
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:30,144
I think they're octopus
and turban snail skewers.

106
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:32,855
THE FUN OF PICKING WHAT THEY WANT

107
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,983
-The tilefish is really good.
-Yeah.

108
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:37,068
How are abalone and hiking related?

109
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:38,861
Related?

110
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:40,571
Delicious…

111
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:43,032
-Delicious?
-Delicious…

112
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:44,534
Hiking is delicious?

113
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:49,580
ABALONE PORRIDGE TO FINISH THE MEAL

114
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:52,709
HOW HIKING AND ABALONE ARE RELATED
ACCORDING TO CAR, THE GARDEN'S CHATGPT

115
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:54,502
1. TAURINE, A KEY TO RECOVERY FROM FATIGUE

116
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:59,132
2. HIGH IN PROTEIN AND LOW IN FAT
TO PREVENT MUSCLE LOSS

117
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:02,552
This is good.
The porridge's really good.

118
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:06,556
3. REPLENISHES MINERALS AND ELECTROLYTES

119
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:10,393
4. ARGININE TO IMPROVE BLOOD FLOW

120
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,812
<i>-Tarzzan found a good restaurant.</i>
<i>-Right.</i>

121
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:15,982
I'm actually a pretty picky eater.

122
00:05:16,065 --> 00:05:16,899
But everything…

123
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,651
-Were you satisfied?
-I was.

124
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,654
Ma'am, could we get the check please?

125
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:22,864
Thank you.

126
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:25,199
-Thank you.
-I'll just pay for it with my fine, okay?

127
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:26,284
Sure.

128
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:29,203
It's 235,000 won.

129
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:30,330
I'll pay in cash.

130
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:31,581
Thank you.

131
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:34,959
I haven't seen anyone
pay with cash in a while.

132
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,210
Thank you for the food.

133
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:38,171
AFTER ENJOYING AN ABALONE FEAST

134
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:41,382
ABALONE RESTAURANT
HAMDEOK BEACH

135
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:44,969
Isn't it beautiful?

136
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:46,679
THEY ARRIVE AT A BEACHFRONT CAFE

137
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:47,805
Let's take a picture.

138
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:48,848
PHOTO TIME ON TERRACE

139
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:49,891
I already set the dial.

140
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,184
What about the flash?

141
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:53,728
One, two, three.

142
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:58,608
Let me take yours.

143
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:01,319
All right. One, two, three.

144
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,413
The water is so clear.

145
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:15,583
Tell me about it.
I feel like I'm on vacation.

146
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:19,670
The color looks amazing.

147
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,923
THE REFRESHING SCENERY
MAKES IT FEEL LIKE VACATION

148
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:24,467
-Let's take a picture.
-I brought a film camera.

149
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:25,885
Really? You brought it?

150
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:26,886
Yeah, just in case.

151
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:28,346
HE BROUGHT IT SINCE IT'S JEJU

152
00:06:28,429 --> 00:06:30,389
Should we do a fist pump? The hiking pose?

153
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:32,558
One, two, three.

154
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,356
Can we take photo booth pictures?

155
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,483
-Sounds great.
-Sounds good.

156
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:43,861
That's perfect
for capturing this nice moment.

157
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:46,906
Hurry.

158
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:48,950
I want to put the photo on my fridge.

159
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:50,368
Now, we're all in it.

160
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:53,830
Look how close we've become.

161
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:56,374
Car-the, try smiling cheerfully.

162
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:57,750
GRINNING

163
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:03,881
-I'm going to put it on my fridge.
-Okay.

164
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,633
-The original?
-Yes, the original.

165
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:08,261
-This will be a nice memory.
-Right, a fond memory.

166
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:09,178
Definitely.

167
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:11,764
Chae-min, you're so handsome.

168
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,474
BUILDING TEAMWORK AND MAKING MEMORIES

169
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:14,725
It came out well.

170
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:16,936
MINISTER OF TRANSPORT RETURNS TO HIS POST

171
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:19,355
I got to take pictures with celebrities.

172
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:21,566
I should be the one saying that.

173
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,693
Where are we going?

174
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:24,944
Big Ball Land.

175
00:07:25,027 --> 00:07:29,574
NEXT IS A MYSTERIOUS ACTIVITY
PRESIDENT TAR DISCOVERED

176
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:32,618
HAMDEOK BEACH
BIG BALL LAND

177
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:36,289
I wish the show
was about going on a trip to Jeju.

178
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:38,207
We were busy chatting
that we came in no time.

179
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,459
THEY ARRIVE AT THE ACTIVITY

180
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:41,335
The balls are huge.

181
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:43,421
-They roll down side by side.
-Is that it?

182
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,964
Don't tell me we have to walk there.

183
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,384
There's no chairlift.

184
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:49,343
ON A HIGH HILL

185
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:51,554
GIANT ORBS

186
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:54,849
TWO PEOPLE CAN RIDE IN EACH BALL

187
00:07:54,932 --> 00:08:00,313
RECREATIONAL SPORT
OF ROLLING DOWN A 300-METER SLOPE

188
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:03,483
IN GIANT ORBS

189
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:07,278
TO PREPARE FOR HIKING HALLASAN

190
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:12,116
PRESIDENT TAR PREPARED THIS ACTIVITY
TO IMPROVE THEIR SENSE OF BALANCE

191
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,910
-Tarzzan, ride with me.
-Okay.

192
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:16,704
And Car-the should ride with Dowoon
so the weights match.

193
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:19,540
And over there…

194
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:24,003
Other shows have filmed here,
and the scenes look almost the same.

195
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:26,923
Can we avoid filming that scene?

196
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:28,925
SIGNS OF OTHER SHOWS THAT CAME BY

197
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:31,344
We should avoid scenes like these.

198
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,596
Don't put in subtitles like this as well.

199
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:34,889
Don't put subtitles at all.

200
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,974
"An exhausted beetle"!

201
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,018
Hello.

202
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:46,984
I feel like those scenes will happen.

203
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:48,986
I don't like it.

204
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:50,696
Just like those classic variety shows.

205
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,198
ACTIVITY-SPECIFIC FILMING EQUIPMENT

206
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:54,408
Like those classic weekend variety shows

207
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:55,952
to entertain viewers.

208
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:56,994
Is this right?

209
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:58,079
PUTS IT RIGHT ON

210
00:08:58,162 --> 00:08:59,497
This is what's funny.

211
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,083
You don't have to
try too hard to be funny.

212
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:03,876
SPREADING LAUGHTER

213
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:07,755
CHAE-MIN AND TARZZAN DEPART FIRST

214
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:11,259
Geez. Who would've thought
we'd ride these?

215
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:13,469
-I've never done this before.
-Me neither.

216
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,429
I didn't expect this.

217
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:16,847
You can get out here.

218
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,391
-Okay.
-Okay. Thank you.

219
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:21,769
CHAE-MIN AND TARZZAN
ARRIVE AT THE STARTING POINT

220
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:24,230
Are you ready?

221
00:09:24,313 --> 00:09:25,189
I am.

222
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:27,108
Hold on. This looks…

223
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,443
We'll be rolling for a while.

224
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:30,653
THEY WILL ROLL DOWN THIS WAY

225
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:32,113
The orbs are bigger than expected.

226
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:33,489
Watch your head.

227
00:09:38,744 --> 00:09:41,747
GET IN

228
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:45,042
What is this?

229
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:47,295
LOSING THEIR SENSE OF BALANCE

230
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:50,339
-Come on, stay still.
-What's wrong?

231
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:52,508
-You are…
-You do it first.

232
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:55,761
ALL SET

233
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:58,306
Dowoon, don't exaggerate your reactions.

234
00:09:58,389 --> 00:10:00,349
-I hate that.
-I never do that.

235
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,351
Rolling down is honestly not that fun.

236
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:05,938
"Gosh, it must be hard for them."
Don't do that.

237
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,232
This is 2026.

238
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:10,484
5 SECONDS BEFORE RELEASE

239
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:13,321
NERVOUS

240
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,474
They're screaming like hell.

241
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:50,107
TARZZAN, CHAE-MIN

242
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,568
CHAOS INSIDE THE ORB

243
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:56,697
LOOKS CALM ON THE OUTSIDE

244
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:58,032
Just film this. It's funny.

245
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:02,161
It's a bit violent.

246
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:05,206
I can't see!

247
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:07,041
Hey, I can't see anything!

248
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:08,751
BEING MERCILESSLY TURNED INSIDE OUT

249
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:09,835
I can't see!

250
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:15,549
ABOUT TO VOMIT THE ABALONE HE ATE

251
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,179
I feel like throwing up.

252
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:21,931
Hold on. Where are we?

253
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:24,350
I feel like throwing up.

254
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:27,603
WHERE? YOU'RE AT THE END

255
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:30,189
DIZZY

256
00:11:30,272 --> 00:11:31,399
You can unstrap and get out.

257
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:32,441
You go first.

258
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:34,318
I'm dizzy.

259
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,821
I'll get out. Be careful.

260
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:46,122
STAGGERING

261
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:48,958
Hi.

262
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:53,879
GETTING OUT IS ALSO NOT EASY

263
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:54,880
Gosh.

264
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:56,966
I feel sick.

265
00:11:58,676 --> 00:11:59,593
Hey, let's…

266
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:01,929
-It's so fun!
-Hey, it's so fun!

267
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:03,556
You have to do this.

268
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:05,141
Seriously!

269
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,976
People sound like that when they lie.

270
00:12:07,643 --> 00:12:10,521
I think we picked the wrong one.

271
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:12,022
Seriously.

272
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:13,691
Hey.

273
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:15,734
Was it fun?

274
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,111
You become so much closer.

275
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,487
Really, it's fun.

276
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:19,613
VERY WORRIED

277
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:21,282
-We got a lot closer.
-Really.

278
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:24,452
I think we can ride that later
when we descend the mountain.

279
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:27,079
Isn't that a good idea?

280
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,664
We can rent them for the day.

281
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:30,374
It'll take an hour less to descend.

282
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,878
I think it'd only take 15 minutes
to come down in those.

283
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:36,172
Then, let's decide after you try it.

284
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,923
-I'll go see how it feels.
-Okay.

285
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,467
-Good luck.
-Good luck.

286
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:41,552
Sir, is this really popular?

287
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:42,678
CAR, THE GARDEN AND DOWOON

288
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:47,308
I'm so curious to see how they'll be
when they come down.

289
00:12:48,642 --> 00:12:51,020
-The heavier one will go to the right.
-That's me.

290
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,605
-Get in?
-Yes.

291
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:53,731
And take off your shoes.

292
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:57,693
Take off your shoes.

293
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,782
To the person on the right,
how much do you weigh?

294
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,117
Almost 100 kg.

295
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:06,619
It's 95 kg.

296
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:07,745
It must be accurate.

297
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:09,705
How about the other?

298
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:12,416
I'm 60… I'm 65 kg.

299
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,835
Strap in your ankles first.

300
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,212
ABOUT 160 KG IN TOTAL

301
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:18,506
CAR, THE GARDEN AND DOWOON ARE READY

302
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:20,341
We'll let the air out a bit more.

303
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:23,969
Since you're heavy, it's dangerous.
We'll deflate it more

304
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:25,221
so it goes slower.

305
00:13:26,013 --> 00:13:29,683
HISSING

306
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:32,311
I'm scared. I'm a bit nervous.

307
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:41,862
Hey, this is…

308
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,824
Hey, this is…

309
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,077
CACKLING

310
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,788
Rolling down is honestly not that fun.

311
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:53,832
SO FUN

312
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,877
DOWOON'S SELF-CAM TURNED OFF
WHILE ROLLING DOWN

313
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:59,755
EVEN WITH LESS AIR, IT'S ROLLING FAST

314
00:13:59,838 --> 00:14:00,965
What is this?

315
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:05,010
-It looks really pathetic from here.
-So pathetic.

316
00:14:06,595 --> 00:14:07,846
What is this?

317
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:11,725
IT LOOKS FUNNY FROM AFAR

318
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:12,726
It's so pitiful.

319
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,019
What on earth is this?

320
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,813
AND IT LOOKS FUNNIER UP CLOSE

321
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:21,777
I told you we shouldn't have done this!

322
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,529
They're saying something.

323
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:25,739
I told you we shouldn't do this!

324
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:29,410
What on earth is this?

325
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:34,790
CAN'T TELL
IF THEY'RE LAUGHING OR SCREAMING

326
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:47,094
AN EXHAUSTED BEETLE

327
00:14:47,177 --> 00:14:48,679
Okay, you've arrived.

328
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:50,472
You can take both hands off.

329
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:52,308
COMPLETELY WORN OUT

330
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:53,726
How was it?

331
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:55,060
I hated it.

332
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:56,312
I'm never doing it again.

333
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,480
-I'm never doing it again.
-I hated it so much.

334
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:01,150
I'm the one who suggested this.
I'm in big trouble now.

335
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:02,568
-I should run away.
-Run.

336
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:03,986
I need to run away.

337
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:10,326
THANKS TO PRESIDENT TAR,
THEIR SENSE OF BALANCE IMPROVED

338
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:13,078
It was something
I'd never experienced before.

339
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:14,580
That's what I felt too.

340
00:15:14,663 --> 00:15:16,123
That was such a strange…

341
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,167
It was a strange feeling.

342
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,382
-You may get out.
-What on earth was that?

343
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,469
The really scary thing was…

344
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:29,678
Before we got in the ball,

345
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:32,014
he was like, "Who's heavier?"

346
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:33,849
"How much do you weigh?"

347
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:34,767
"I weigh 90--"

348
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,602
-"It must be accurate."
-We got the same.

349
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,896
I mean, that was so sudden and scary.

350
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,481
"Tell me the exact number!"

351
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:41,523
Why are you crying?

352
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:43,025
"We need to deflate it."

353
00:15:43,108 --> 00:15:44,193
He's crying.

354
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:45,694
"You can't roll down like this."

355
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:48,197
-You felt sick, right?
-He said to me,

356
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,907
"I told you I didn't want to do it!"

357
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:55,079
We're finally going home.

358
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:57,498
Seriously, in those big orbs…

359
00:15:57,581 --> 00:15:59,458
Didn't you feel like throwing up?

360
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:01,502
Just as you said,
we came down so pathetically.

361
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:03,837
You can't help it. You're strapped in.

362
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:05,005
It was so bouncy.

363
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,882
I feel so drained too.

364
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:09,134
MOVING TO BASE CAMP

365
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:11,971
BIG BALL LAND
BASE CAMP

366
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:14,098
After all that fun,
it's still 3:30 p.m.

367
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:16,433
We must have arrived in Jeju really early.

368
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,643
A LAZY AFTERNOON IN JEJU

369
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:21,730
It's so cloudy only around Hallasan.

370
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,440
-Where's Hallasan?
-Is that it?

371
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:24,942
That's Hallasan? No way.

372
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,568
Over there. Way in the distance.

373
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:28,362
Not this one, right?

374
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:29,863
No, the one in the distance.

375
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:32,366
IT'S BECOME CLOUDY AROUND HALLASAN

376
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:35,536
THE WEATHER AROUND BAENGNOKDAM
CHANGES RAPIDLY

377
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:40,457
WILL THEY BE ABLE TO SEE
BAENGNOKDAM TOMORROW?

378
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:43,836
I bet it'll be cold in the morning.

379
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:45,504
Probably so.

380
00:16:45,587 --> 00:16:46,880
I bet it'll be very windy.

381
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:49,216
But compared to the mountains we've hiked,

382
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:51,844
I think it will be much warmer.

383
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:00,352
-It's like a whole town.
-This kind of vibe?

384
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,438
There are even vans.

385
00:17:02,521 --> 00:17:04,523
THEY ARRIVE AT BASE CAMP

386
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:06,525
There are even limousines here.

387
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:07,943
Gosh, limousines.

388
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:14,116
Gosh, it looks amazing.

389
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:17,161
Will we get breakfast too?

390
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:22,082
WITH HALLASAN BEHIND THEM IN THE DISTANCE

391
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,086
THEIR JEJU ISLAND BASE CAMP

392
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:27,921
I suddenly feel excited.

393
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:31,175
ENTERING IN A GOOD MOOD

394
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:34,803
LOBBY

395
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,431
There's no elevator?

396
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:38,807
Is this training for hiking?

397
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:47,232
What is this place? There are even drums.

398
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,485
Dowoon, this is a place for you.

399
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:52,404
I know. Should we play
"My Whole World," Jung-won?

400
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:57,868
This will be so fun!
I want to play music together.

401
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,420
LIVING ROOM

402
00:18:09,379 --> 00:18:11,548
KITCHEN

403
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:17,930
THERE'S EVEN A SECOND FLOOR

404
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:22,434
DESCEND CLUB CHECKS IN

405
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:24,937
The living room is mine.

406
00:18:25,437 --> 00:18:27,439
DOWOON TAKES THE LIVING ROOM AGAIN

407
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:29,525
Shouldn't we play some live music here?

408
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:31,401
It's all set up.

409
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,820
GOES AS IF DRAWN TO THE DRUMS

410
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:34,446
This is nice.

411
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:35,697
SITS DOWN WITH FAMILIAR EASE

412
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:36,698
Dowoon's on the drums.

413
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,619
AUTOMATICALLY PRODUCES A BEAT

414
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:45,415
THIS IS THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT'S
REAL JOB

415
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:48,001
He's already started playing the drums.

416
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:51,797
THE END

417
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,173
Why did you stop?

418
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,843
Hey, play something for us.

419
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,095
Play something without copyright issues.

420
00:18:58,178 --> 00:18:59,263
Without copyright issues?

421
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:02,558
THE IMPROMPTU PERFORMANCE BEGINS

422
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:11,942
<i>Why do we go hiking?</i>

423
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,527
<i>I have no idea</i>

424
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:14,653
He's just freestyling.

425
00:19:14,736 --> 00:19:16,738
FREESTYLE RAPPING OVER THE DRUM BEAT

426
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:18,198
<i>Why do we go hiking?</i>

427
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:21,118
PUTS THE HIKING STICKS DOWN
TO PICK UP DRUM STICKS

428
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,119
This is fun.

429
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:24,246
-Car-the needs to come here now.
-Car-the.

430
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:30,419
YOU'VE BECOME MY WHOLE WORLD

431
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:34,798
MIMICS CAR, THE GARDEN
WHILE HE'S NOT HERE

432
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:42,389
THE SONG'S WRITER IS STILL CHECKING IN

433
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:43,307
"TREE"

434
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:45,642
ORIGINAL ARTIST: CAR, THE GARDEN
DRUMS: DOWOON

435
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:47,477
VOCALS: TARZZAN
REACTIONS: LEE CHAE-MIN

436
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:53,192
A SONG BY A SINGER WHO LOVES NATURE

437
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:59,448
IT WILL BE SUNG WITHOUT HIM

438
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:05,579
VOCALS BY TARZZAN

439
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:07,956
This is amazing.

440
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:12,002
NOT EVEN HIS SONG
BUT CAN PLAY WITHOUT SHEET MUSIC

441
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,838
THE SONG'S WRITER
IS TOO PREOCCUPIED WITH CHECKING IN

442
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:18,258
TAKES A ROOM WITH A TREE PAINTING

443
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:22,179
CAR, THE GARDEN'S SONG
WITHOUT CAR, THE GARDEN

444
00:20:22,262 --> 00:20:24,056
GOING FOR EMOTIONS OVER SKILLS

445
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:26,767
This song is so difficult to sing.

446
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:32,773
IT'S EASIER TO EXPRESS WITH HIS BODY

447
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:37,069
THE CAR, THE GARDEN-LESS PERFORMANCE ENDS

448
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:39,863
Why isn't Car-the coming?

449
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:43,408
I'M HERE

450
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:47,704
AFTER TAKING HIS TIME TUNING THE GUITAR

451
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:51,833
HIKING: IMPOSSIBLE

452
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:56,213
SINGING, WRITING LYRICS, COMPOSING,
PLAYING GUITAR AND PIANO: POSSIBLE

453
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:58,966
HE WANTS TO CAPTURE HIM
DOING HIS DAY JOB

454
00:21:00,008 --> 00:21:01,051
He's so cool.

455
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:06,348
HE LOOKS COOL EXCEPT WHEN HE'S HIKING

456
00:21:07,724 --> 00:21:12,980
AND SO, THE DAY ENDS

457
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:18,110
AND THE TIME TO CLIMB UP HALLASAN
COMES CLOSER AND CLOSER

458
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:20,112
THE MEMBERS ARE GATHERED
IN THE DINING ROOM

459
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:22,114
I like the vibe here.

460
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,740
Here's the plan for Hallasan

461
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:24,950
to reach Baengnokdam.

462
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,368
PLANNING THEIR SECOND HIKE

463
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:27,869
First off, tomorrow,

464
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,038
we'll climb up separately

465
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:31,581
and meet up at the top.

466
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:33,000
-That's the goal.
-Right.

467
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:34,918
WHY DO WE HIKE?

468
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:36,086
WHY DO WE HIKE SEPARATELY?

469
00:21:36,169 --> 00:21:37,212
Go separately in pairs?

470
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:38,839
You'll hike in pairs this time.

471
00:21:38,922 --> 00:21:41,300
There are two trails
you can take to Baengnokdam.

472
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:45,387
2 DIFFERENT TRAILS TO BAENGNOKDAM

473
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,556
BAENGNOKDAM

474
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:51,018
SEONGPANAK TRAIL, GWANEUMSA TRAIL

475
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:52,853
I'm sure you got the reservation text.

476
00:21:52,936 --> 00:21:55,981
Since Jung-won and Chae-min
are a bit injured,

477
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:57,149
we thought…

478
00:21:57,232 --> 00:21:58,400
KNEE INJURY, WRIST INJURY

479
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:01,069
…the two nursing injuries
should take the Seongpanak trail,

480
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,571
which is a bit easier.

481
00:22:04,448 --> 00:22:06,575
THE SEONGPANAK TRAIL
IS LESS STEEP BUT LONGER

482
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:09,619
EASY FOR EVEN BEGINNERS TO TRY

483
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:13,415
SEONGPANAK TRAIL
DIFFICULTY: MODERATE

484
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:16,376
What was the trail
for the normal people again?

485
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:18,795
-The Gwaneumsa Trail.
-That's for the normal people?

486
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,339
"Normal people"!

487
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:25,719
THE GWANEUMSA TRAIL HAS HELLISH STAIRS

488
00:22:25,802 --> 00:22:29,473
THE EXTREME INCLINE TESTS YOUR LIMITS

489
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:32,309
GWANEUMSA TRAIL
DIFFICULTY: HARD

490
00:22:32,392 --> 00:22:35,270
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST 2-ON-2 HIKE

491
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:37,564
We've already decided when to wake up.

492
00:22:37,647 --> 00:22:39,858
-Wake up at 5:20 a.m.
-At 5:20 a.m.

493
00:22:39,941 --> 00:22:41,401
1. WAKE UP AT 5:20 A.M.

494
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:43,945
Then, what time do we leave from here?

495
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,072
At 6:00 a.m.

496
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:46,823
2. LEAVE BASE CAMP AT 6:00 A.M.

497
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:49,618
It'll take about an hour
to get there, right?

498
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:52,037
We'll drop these two off first.

499
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:55,749
<i>If we leave at 6:00 a.m.,</i>
<i>will we drop them off at around 6:40 a.m.?</i>

500
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:57,667
3. GWANEUMSA TEAM ARRIVES AT 6:40 A.M.

501
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:59,211
<i>Write down, "Drop off at 6:40 a.m."</i>

502
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:01,379
4. SEONGPANAK TEAM ARRIVES AT 7:00 A.M.

503
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:03,465
THEN EACH PAIR BEGINS HIKING THEIR TRAIL

504
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:07,344
So our mission
is just to see Baengnokdam, right?

505
00:23:07,427 --> 00:23:10,055
-Right.
-Just climb up to see it? Okay.

506
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:11,556
JUST CLIMB UP?

507
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:17,604
2 RESTRICTIONS ON HIKING HALLASAN

508
00:23:17,687 --> 00:23:21,566
-You have to leave the summit by 1:30 p.m.
-Start climbing down?

509
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:22,526
FIRST RESTRICTION

510
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:24,653
THEY MUST ARRIVE AT BAENGNOKDAM
BEFORE 1:30 P.M.

511
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:28,490
THERE'S ALSO A MYTH ABOUT BAENGNOKDAM…

512
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:31,743
"ONLY EXTREMELY LUCKY PEOPLE
CAN SEE BAENGNOKDAM"

513
00:23:33,161 --> 00:23:35,997
SECOND RESTRICTION
FICKLE WEATHER AROUND BAENGNOKDAM

514
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:39,668
THEY NEED TO BE LUCKY WITH THE WEATHER
AND METICULOUSLY CALCULATE HIKING TIME

515
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:42,254
Then, according to our plan,

516
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:46,633
we will stay on the summit

517
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:48,802
for no more than five minutes.

518
00:23:49,344 --> 00:23:51,388
MANAGER CAR IS FIRM

519
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:53,765
Only five minutes at the top.
I'm telling the crew.

520
00:23:54,349 --> 00:23:56,059
We'll shoot it and climb down right away.

521
00:23:56,143 --> 00:23:59,604
What if we can see Baengnokdam clearly?
What if it's really beautiful?

522
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,982
-Then, let's make it ten minutes.
-Yeah, ten minutes.

523
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,817
Only if there are no clouds.

524
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:06,361
-If it's cloudy, go right away.
-If so, then five minutes.

525
00:24:06,444 --> 00:24:08,488
-Eight minutes.
-Eight.

526
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:09,489
COMPROMISING GARDEN

527
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:11,491
-Meet halfway at eight? Okay.
-Halfway is good.

528
00:24:12,075 --> 00:24:13,660
There's something I want to do.

529
00:24:13,743 --> 00:24:14,578
What is it?

530
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:15,912
Well,

531
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:18,915
you and I can make
a big heart in the back,

532
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:21,668
and you two can make
a small one like this in front.

533
00:24:21,751 --> 00:24:23,211
DOWOON'S ADDITIONAL SUGGESTION

534
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:24,212
Sure.

535
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,922
-Sure. Like this?
-I want to do that.

536
00:24:26,006 --> 00:24:27,507
But why do you suddenly want to?

537
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:29,926
-It'll make us look happy.
-Okay, good.

538
00:24:30,010 --> 00:24:32,596
Okay, we'll take a photo of the hearts.
Make it nine minutes.

539
00:24:32,679 --> 00:24:34,389
SHOCKINGLY, HE ACCEPTS THE SUGGESTION

540
00:24:36,266 --> 00:24:38,768
We brought a Polaroid camera.
Do you want it?

541
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,562
Actually, I brought one too.

542
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:44,566
I brought it just in case I wanted
to capture the moment.

543
00:24:44,649 --> 00:24:46,526
We can use it for our heart photo.

544
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:48,111
I'll use that then.

545
00:24:48,195 --> 00:24:49,154
-Yes.
-Good.

546
00:24:49,237 --> 00:24:50,697
THINGS TO DO AT SUMMIT FOR 9 MINUTES

547
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:52,449
1. SEE BAENGNOKDAM
2. GROUP POLAROID PHOTO

548
00:24:52,532 --> 00:24:53,825
Are there any fines to pay?

549
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:55,493
Is the fine rule still valid?

550
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:56,578
It is.

551
00:24:56,661 --> 00:24:57,954
He basically pays it regularly.

552
00:24:58,038 --> 00:24:59,539
NEGATIVE COMMENT: 300,000-WON FINE

553
00:24:59,623 --> 00:25:02,167
If you're fined again,
we won't have to pay anything.

554
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,002
Most likely.

555
00:25:04,669 --> 00:25:07,589
HALLASAN HIKING PLAN COMPLETE

556
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:11,426
Can our audio director check this out?

557
00:25:11,509 --> 00:25:13,678
You don't have to use it
if you don't like it.

558
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:15,180
USE WHAT?

559
00:25:15,263 --> 00:25:16,598
Really? I see.

560
00:25:16,681 --> 00:25:19,184
A BREAK DURING THE SEORAKSAN HIKE

561
00:25:20,810 --> 00:25:22,020
Are you all right?

562
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:23,647
My gosh.

563
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:26,399
This could break your back.
This is madness.

564
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:29,194
DOWOON WAS SHOCKED BY THE WEIGHT
OF THE AUDIO EQUIPMENT

565
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:30,195
What is?

566
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:31,738
Try carrying this.

567
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:32,948
Are you okay?

568
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:35,617
DOWOON KEPT WORRYING
ABOUT THE AUDIO DIRECTOR

569
00:25:35,700 --> 00:25:36,952
I ordered something

570
00:25:37,035 --> 00:25:39,120
for our audio director.

571
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,456
-What?
-A walking assist device.

572
00:25:41,539 --> 00:25:43,750
Just wait. I ordered something.

573
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:46,378
You use it first. Seriously.

574
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:49,673
HE SENT A WALKING ASSIST DEVICE AS A GIFT

575
00:25:50,465 --> 00:25:53,260
UNBOXING THE GIFT

576
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:56,554
WALKING ASSIST DEVICE FOR HIKING

577
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:59,182
REDUCES STRAIN ON LEGS WHILE WALKING

578
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:02,102
ADJUST THE BELT FIRST

579
00:26:03,144 --> 00:26:05,563
AND STRAP IN THE THIGHS FIRMLY AS WELL

580
00:26:05,647 --> 00:26:09,109
IT GENTLY ASSISTS THE LEGS WHEN WALKING

581
00:26:10,110 --> 00:26:10,944
Is that it?

582
00:26:11,027 --> 00:26:12,529
That's the walking assist device?

583
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:15,657
Does it help?

584
00:26:17,575 --> 00:26:19,244
But if I use this,

585
00:26:19,327 --> 00:26:21,121
I'll have to carry the battery too.

586
00:26:21,204 --> 00:26:22,580
ADDITIONAL WEIGHT THANKS TO DOWOON

587
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:23,915
That's one more thing to carry.

588
00:26:24,499 --> 00:26:26,126
Do you walk around like a robot?

589
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:29,129
-That's right.
-Really?

590
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:31,131
The motor helps lift the legs.

591
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:33,258
You're not lifting them?

592
00:26:33,341 --> 00:26:34,634
It's not me.

593
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:37,512
If you lift a little,
the device lifts it all the way up.

594
00:26:37,595 --> 00:26:38,930
-Like this.
-That's great.

595
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:40,640
Hear the whirring sound?

596
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:44,394
THE AUDIO DIRECTOR'S UNBELIEVABLE REVIEW

597
00:26:44,477 --> 00:26:46,438
This is hard to believe.

598
00:26:47,022 --> 00:26:49,858
How is it when climbing stairs?
Like going two steps at a time.

599
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:52,569
Of course, it helps to climb stairs.

600
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:54,779
Is it definitely easier?

601
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:58,116
It is. When climbing up,
it lifts the legs up.

602
00:26:58,992 --> 00:27:00,618
LIFTING HIGH

603
00:27:01,244 --> 00:27:02,829
HIS MOVEMENTS ARE HARD TO BELIEVE

604
00:27:02,912 --> 00:27:04,289
It looks so unnatural.

605
00:27:04,372 --> 00:27:05,623
He's walking like a robot.

606
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,459
AUTOMATICALLY ON ROBOT MODE

607
00:27:07,542 --> 00:27:09,419
You can't stop midway.

608
00:27:09,502 --> 00:27:11,296
Your leg keeps going
until it stops lifting.

609
00:27:11,379 --> 00:27:12,881
Then, you have to walk up like this?

610
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:14,215
It feels a bit like that.

611
00:27:15,675 --> 00:27:18,178
-It has to go up to here.
-Honestly, this should be enough.

612
00:27:18,261 --> 00:27:19,262
-But like this?
-Yes.

613
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:20,180
WITH MORE ENERGY

614
00:27:20,263 --> 00:27:21,431
You have to go two at a time.

615
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:22,807
I'm curious.

616
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:24,517
Can I try it?

617
00:27:24,601 --> 00:27:26,102
CHAE-MIN TRIES IT HIMSELF

618
00:27:26,186 --> 00:27:29,731
To be honest, I'm thinking
he exaggerated a bit.

619
00:27:29,814 --> 00:27:31,024
I think he was acting.

620
00:27:31,858 --> 00:27:33,193
Do you feel something?

621
00:27:33,276 --> 00:27:34,944
Something suddenly grabbed onto me.

622
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:36,529
I'll try walking now.

623
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:41,451
What are you, a robot?

624
00:27:41,534 --> 00:27:43,036
AWKWARD SINCE IT'S HIS FIRST TIME

625
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:44,871
Try walking naturally.

626
00:27:46,247 --> 00:27:47,832
No, you can't help it.

627
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:49,834
YOUR LEGS DON'T MOVE THE WAY YOU WANT

628
00:27:49,918 --> 00:27:51,586
HEADS TOWARD THE STAIRS

629
00:27:51,669 --> 00:27:52,712
Is it comfortable?

630
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:54,923
LIKE A SOLDIER

631
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:56,716
EVEN MORE AWKWARD

632
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:57,759
Chae-min, come on.

633
00:27:57,842 --> 00:28:00,053
-He's exaggerating.
-Don't try to be funny.

634
00:28:00,136 --> 00:28:01,221
I'M NOT

635
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:02,514
Hold on.

636
00:28:02,597 --> 00:28:05,683
IT'S THE SAME WHEN WALKING DOWN AS WELL

637
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:07,602
CHAE-MIN MOVES MORE AWKWARDLY AS HE GOES

638
00:28:07,685 --> 00:28:08,937
He's acting.

639
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:10,021
I'm not.

640
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:12,065
Chae-min, give it to me. Let me try it.

641
00:28:12,148 --> 00:28:14,442
-This is for real!
-Come on.

642
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:16,361
-How do you stop it?
-It's really like this!

643
00:28:17,237 --> 00:28:19,280
It's really like this. I think…

644
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:21,574
Hey, tyrant. Nice acting.

645
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:22,617
FRUSTRATED TYRANT

646
00:28:22,700 --> 00:28:24,327
-You're a good actor.
-No, it's not that.

647
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:25,787
Do you want to try it?

648
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:27,330
Seriously, it wasn't on purpose.

649
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,833
-Turn it off first.
-I wasn't trying to be funny.

650
00:28:31,209 --> 00:28:32,419
It feels tight now.

651
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:34,254
THE ONE WHO PAID FOR IT TRIES

652
00:28:34,337 --> 00:28:35,672
Try lifting your legs.

653
00:28:35,755 --> 00:28:37,465
One by one. Keep going.

654
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:39,759
-What? So this is what happens.
-What? Come on.

655
00:28:39,843 --> 00:28:42,137
I TOLD YOU

656
00:28:42,762 --> 00:28:44,305
You really do walk like this.

657
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:45,890
Hold on. But…

658
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:48,268
Wait. I'll try walking
as if I'm really I'm hiking.

659
00:28:49,811 --> 00:28:50,812
This is good.

660
00:28:53,189 --> 00:28:55,608
Relax and lift your legs,
and they shoot up.

661
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:57,152
If I lift my legs, it pulls them up.

662
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:58,069
IF LEGS RELAX

663
00:28:58,153 --> 00:28:59,612
MOVES LIKE A ROBOT

664
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:00,739
It makes you walk weird.

665
00:29:01,531 --> 00:29:02,949
It makes you walk weird.

666
00:29:03,533 --> 00:29:06,244
MY OWN TWO LEGS FEEL UNFAMILIAR

667
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:09,164
THE SUSPICIOUS CAR-THE TRIES IT ON TOO

668
00:29:09,873 --> 00:29:11,040
KICKING THE AIR

669
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,292
Oh, it's not on yet.

670
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:13,418
Come on, man.

671
00:29:13,501 --> 00:29:14,919
That was a bit lame.

672
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:16,296
It was kind of lame, Jung-won.

673
00:29:16,379 --> 00:29:17,672
I'm so disappointed.

674
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:18,923
EMBARRASSED

675
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:20,425
I wanted everyone to laugh.

676
00:29:20,508 --> 00:29:21,760
TRYING AGAIN

677
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:22,969
I can feel it.

678
00:29:23,052 --> 00:29:24,637
Try walking fast.

679
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:26,181
Okay. It's on?

680
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:27,390
Lift your legs fast.

681
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:31,352
LOOKING MORE ENERGETIC

682
00:29:31,436 --> 00:29:32,437
Try the stairs.

683
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:33,688
The straps came undone.

684
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:35,982
What the heck? Look at this!

685
00:29:36,065 --> 00:29:38,234
Hey, AI's rebelling!

686
00:29:38,943 --> 00:29:40,236
What the heck? Look at this!

687
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:42,739
THE WALKING ASSIST DEVICE
REJECTS ITS NEW OWNER

688
00:29:42,822 --> 00:29:44,532
-It's really moving.
-AI's rebelling.

689
00:29:45,241 --> 00:29:46,701
Hey, what's going on?

690
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:53,416
THE DEVICE IS HARD TO TAME

691
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:54,918
You little punk.

692
00:29:55,001 --> 00:29:55,877
Stay still.

693
00:29:57,170 --> 00:29:58,546
Why are you doing this to only me?

694
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:00,089
Let's work together.

695
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,550
Don't be angry. Okay, let's go.

696
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:04,511
-Let's go. Hey!
-Try the stairs.

697
00:30:05,136 --> 00:30:06,930
ANOTHER TANTRUM

698
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:10,433
LOL

699
00:30:10,517 --> 00:30:11,351
This little punk!

700
00:30:11,434 --> 00:30:13,061
PRODUCT REVIEW
IT HATES CAR, THE GARDEN

701
00:30:13,144 --> 00:30:14,604
Stay still. I clearly told you.

702
00:30:14,687 --> 00:30:15,772
A CHAOTIC ENDING

703
00:30:15,855 --> 00:30:17,398
Anyway, thank you so much, Dowoon.

704
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:18,817
-No worries.
-Seriously.

705
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:20,193
HE THANKS HIM SINCERELY

706
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:23,571
It shows how caring Dowoon is.
That's what's important.

707
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:25,323
This is embarrassing. Let's wash up.

708
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:28,326
-Thank you, everyone.
-Thank you.

709
00:30:28,409 --> 00:30:31,454
NEXT MORNING

710
00:30:32,455 --> 00:30:33,331
The backpack…

711
00:30:33,414 --> 00:30:35,416
The backpack gets in the way.

712
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:37,710
UP AND DOWN

713
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:40,880
SADLY, HE WASN'T ABLE TO WEAR THE DEVICE

714
00:30:40,964 --> 00:30:42,298
Try to adjust the bag.

715
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:44,133
Let's wash up and go to bed.

716
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:46,386
-Okay.
-Good job, everyone.

717
00:30:47,887 --> 00:30:50,306
-What's that?
-I bought them in the US.

718
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:52,141
TARZZAN BRINGS SOMETHING OUT

719
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:54,310
These are utensils for hiking.

720
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:55,270
Did you make them?

721
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:58,731
No, I just saw them
and ordered some for you too.

722
00:30:58,815 --> 00:31:01,067
-Gosh, thank you.
-Sure.

723
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:03,444
And these are lip balms.

724
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:05,989
You can each pick one.

725
00:31:06,656 --> 00:31:08,950
CUTE LIP BALMS FROM THE US

726
00:31:09,033 --> 00:31:12,078
CHOCOLATE ENERGY BARS
WITH PACKAGING PERFECT FOR HIKING

727
00:31:12,996 --> 00:31:16,708
A BRAND NEW BACKPACK

728
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:19,919
-What are you doing?
-What?

729
00:31:20,003 --> 00:31:22,380
-What are you doing?
-It's my first time trying this bag.

730
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:24,632
You bought a new one?

731
00:31:24,716 --> 00:31:25,717
Yeah.

732
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:28,177
SOMEWHAT EMBARRASSED

733
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:31,973
PACKING TRAIL FOOD ONE BY ONE

734
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:35,143
FOR TARZZAN

735
00:31:35,935 --> 00:31:37,312
THESE ARE FOR ME

736
00:31:37,395 --> 00:31:39,355
YOON DORAEMON PACKS PLENTY

737
00:31:39,939 --> 00:31:42,984
HE PACKS CUP NOODLES
AND UTENSILS FOR LUNCH AS WELL

738
00:31:44,527 --> 00:31:48,281
THEY FINALLY GO TO BED

739
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:51,618
We usually have late-night snacks
around this hour.

740
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:52,785
I know.

741
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:53,828
Seriously.

742
00:31:54,662 --> 00:31:57,665
EVERYONE GOES TO BED

743
00:31:59,959 --> 00:32:01,836
-Good night.
-Good night.

744
00:32:10,178 --> 00:32:12,305
CURRENT TIME

745
00:32:13,681 --> 00:32:18,269
CHAE-MIN WAKES UP

746
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:22,357
HE'S THE FIRST TO WAKE UP AS ALWAYS

747
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,859
Did you sleep well?

748
00:32:24,943 --> 00:32:25,902
I slept really well.

749
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:27,362
-Really?
-Yeah.

750
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:31,616
DILIGENTLY STARTS HIS MORNING
WITH AN APPLE

751
00:32:32,533 --> 00:32:35,787
Why do I suddenly feel scared?
I have a feeling that it'll be tough.

752
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:40,375
MEANWHILE, CAR, THE GARDEN
IS ALREADY GETTING DRESSED

753
00:32:41,084 --> 00:32:42,210
Someone's coming down.

754
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:45,088
-Good morning.
-Morning.

755
00:32:45,672 --> 00:32:47,590
He's already dressed.

756
00:32:48,216 --> 00:32:50,009
HE COMPLAINS BUT GETS READY THE FASTEST

757
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:52,053
-You slept right away, right?
-Yes.

758
00:32:52,136 --> 00:32:54,263
-I slept so well.
-Right.

759
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:57,183
-Were you feeling good when we left?
-Yes, I was.

760
00:32:58,351 --> 00:33:00,311
A good night's sleep definitely helped.

761
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:03,272
It honestly meant one less excuse to make.

762
00:33:03,856 --> 00:33:05,108
LEAVING BASE CAMP

763
00:33:05,191 --> 00:33:06,776
-Let's go.
-Let's check the weather.

764
00:33:07,318 --> 00:33:08,903
Okay. What's with the weather?

765
00:33:09,404 --> 00:33:11,489
What's with the weather? It's not cold.

766
00:33:11,572 --> 00:33:16,536
CURRENT TEMPERATURE: -3°C
WIND SPEED: LIGHT

767
00:33:16,619 --> 00:33:18,371
We won't need padded jackets.

768
00:33:18,454 --> 00:33:20,289
-3°C DOESN'T FEEL COLD FOR THEM NOW

769
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:21,833
Seat belts, please.

770
00:33:21,916 --> 00:33:23,626
Everyone buckled up?

771
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:24,919
Let's go.

772
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:26,504
HEADING FOR HALLASAN

773
00:33:27,088 --> 00:33:30,550
I think there will be
more people on our trail.

774
00:33:30,633 --> 00:33:32,093
-Since it's easier?
-Yeah.

775
00:33:32,927 --> 00:33:34,971
SEONGPANAK TRAIL
DIFFICULTY: MODERATE

776
00:33:35,555 --> 00:33:38,433
Apparently, ours won't be harder
than Seoraksan.

777
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:42,061
GWANEUMSA TRAIL
DIFFICULTY: HARD

778
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:43,813
We're here.

779
00:33:45,481 --> 00:33:47,483
We're here. I think you'll start here.

780
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,694
THEY ARRIVE
AT THE GWANEUMSA TRAIL PARKING LOT

781
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:54,240
THE SUN HASN'T EVEN RISEN YET

782
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:59,203
THE CAWING OF CROWS
ECHOES THROUGH THE PARKING LOT

783
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,790
ALONG WITH A PERSON'S ROAR

784
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:06,002
HE BEGINS THE DAY WITH A ROAR

785
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:08,129
Bye, Chae-min.

786
00:34:08,212 --> 00:34:09,047
Good luck!

787
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:10,715
-See you later.
-Be safe.

788
00:34:10,798 --> 00:34:12,216
-See you, guys.
-See you.

789
00:34:12,300 --> 00:34:13,342
Bye.

790
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:15,094
THE CARING DESCEND CLUB

791
00:34:15,178 --> 00:34:16,596
See you at the top.

792
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:18,973
Good luck.

793
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:20,725
-Good luck.
-Bye. Be safe.

794
00:34:20,808 --> 00:34:21,976
You too.

795
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:25,563
CAR, THE GARDEN AND CHAE-MIN
HEAD FOR SEONGPANAK

796
00:34:25,646 --> 00:34:26,939
PUTTING ON CRAMPONS

797
00:34:27,023 --> 00:34:29,484
Did you ever imagine
you and I would take on

798
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:30,985
a more difficult trail?

799
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:33,071
A BIT JEALOUS

800
00:34:33,154 --> 00:34:35,364
Next time, I'm coming in injured.

801
00:34:36,240 --> 00:34:37,658
I plan to be hurt next week.

802
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:40,536
THE TWO WITHOUT INJURIES WILL TAKE

803
00:34:40,620 --> 00:34:43,664
GWANEUMSA TRAIL

804
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:52,507
THE TRAIL WHERE YOU CAN ENJOY
THE NATURAL SCENERY OF HALLASAN

805
00:34:58,679 --> 00:35:00,139
8.7 KM OF HIKING TO BAENGNOKDAM

806
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:02,558
HIKING TIME: ABOUT 5 HOURS

807
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:07,563
AND THEY WILL TAKE
SEONGPANAK TRAIL TO DESCEND

808
00:35:07,647 --> 00:35:10,441
MODERATE SECTION FOR 1 HOUR

809
00:35:10,525 --> 00:35:13,569
HARD SECTION FOR 2 HOURS AND 20 MINUTES

810
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:16,614
EASY SECTION FOR 20 MINUTES

811
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:19,617
HARD SECTION FOR 1 HOUR AND 20 MINUTES

812
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:23,746
THE TRAIL IS NOTORIOUSLY TOUGH

813
00:35:23,830 --> 00:35:25,414
Did you warm up?

814
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:27,792
Well, we will on the way.

815
00:35:27,875 --> 00:35:28,793
Yeah, on the way.

816
00:35:28,876 --> 00:35:30,169
GWANEUMSA TEAM DEPARTS

817
00:35:30,253 --> 00:35:32,463
It's 7:18 a.m. now.

818
00:35:33,923 --> 00:35:35,967
There's a police officer here.

819
00:35:36,050 --> 00:35:39,387
To prevent illegal activities
or people from going off-trail,

820
00:35:39,470 --> 00:35:41,430
they're stationed here.

821
00:35:41,514 --> 00:35:43,224
I feel so grateful for them.

822
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:45,017
Hello.

823
00:35:45,101 --> 00:35:47,061
-Hello.
-Hello.

824
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:50,231
Oh, right. I need to take out my wallet.

825
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:53,151
THEY ARRIVE AT THE ENTRANCE

826
00:35:56,863 --> 00:35:59,782
ONLY 500 PEOPLE A DAY CAN ENTER
GWANEUMSA WITH RESERVATIONS

827
00:36:00,366 --> 00:36:01,367
Here it is.

828
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:02,618
1. SHOW ID

829
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:04,162
Show me the QR code as well.

830
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:05,872
2. SHOW QR CODE

831
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:06,789
You may enter.

832
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:08,541
-Thank you.
-Have a nice day.

833
00:36:08,624 --> 00:36:12,420
THEY PASS THROUGH THE ENTRANCE

834
00:36:13,004 --> 00:36:13,838
I feel hot.

835
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:17,175
There sure is a temperature difference.

836
00:36:17,967 --> 00:36:20,553
CURRENTLY -2.9°C
IT FEELS RELATIVELY WARM

837
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:24,599
HIKING AS A PAIR FOR THE FIRST TIME

838
00:36:25,183 --> 00:36:28,686
FLAT IN THE BEGINNING

839
00:36:29,353 --> 00:36:31,981
LEAD: TARZZAN

840
00:36:32,064 --> 00:36:34,984
TAIL: DOWOON

841
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,571
IN FORMATION AS A PAIR TOO

842
00:36:39,488 --> 00:36:42,200
It's quite rocky here too.

843
00:36:42,283 --> 00:36:43,618
It's actually basalt here.

844
00:36:43,701 --> 00:36:44,744
You're right.

845
00:36:44,827 --> 00:36:47,205
SINCE THE MOUNTAIN WAS FORMED
BY VOLCANIC ERUPTIONS

846
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:50,917
BASALT IS EVERYWHERE

847
00:36:51,500 --> 00:36:52,752
This is a rocky mountain too.

848
00:36:53,586 --> 00:36:56,005
THERE ARE A LOT OF ROCKS
SO HE'S NOT WRONG

849
00:36:56,964 --> 00:36:58,049
It's a volcano.

850
00:36:58,132 --> 00:36:59,383
Right, it's a volcano.

851
00:37:00,676 --> 00:37:03,095
<i>It was fun to see basalt.</i>

852
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:06,390
It was everywhere on the ground
since it was a volcano.

853
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:07,892
That was…

854
00:37:07,975 --> 00:37:09,477
It was… fun.

855
00:37:10,269 --> 00:37:11,562
LAUGHING

856
00:37:11,646 --> 00:37:14,398
LOOKING AROUND

857
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:15,650
What's this?

858
00:37:17,902 --> 00:37:20,446
SURROUNDING THE TRAIL

859
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:22,823
THIS IS…

860
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,033
It's bamboo.

861
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:25,701
Bamboo?

862
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:28,287
-It's bamboo.
-Bamboo? Really?

863
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:30,623
They're broadleaf bamboo.
They're called <i>joritdae.</i>

864
00:37:30,706 --> 00:37:32,166
DWARF SPECIES OF BAMBOO

865
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:35,336
You'll see them everywhere
while hiking Hallasan.

866
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:39,799
Isn't the scenery here
totally different from the others?

867
00:37:39,882 --> 00:37:40,925
Totally.

868
00:37:41,509 --> 00:37:43,552
TARZZAN ENJOYS THE SCENERY

869
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:45,763
AND THE DOCENT ENJOYS EXPLAINING

870
00:37:45,846 --> 00:37:47,765
This says "Gwaneumsa 5-1," right?

871
00:37:47,848 --> 00:37:48,683
-Yes.
-Yes.

872
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:52,270
It means Gwaneumsa
is the fifth trail on Hallasan,

873
00:37:52,353 --> 00:37:54,355
and this number changes every 250 m.

874
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:56,649
This "one" means we've come 250 m.

875
00:38:01,821 --> 00:38:03,864
If you see "5-34,"

876
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:06,117
you're on the summit.

877
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:08,703
You can tell
how much you've climbed from that.

878
00:38:08,786 --> 00:38:10,037
Okay. So, each number is 250 m.

879
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:11,580
JUST WHEN IT SEEMED THEY WERE GOING…

880
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:14,125
Right, this spot.

881
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:17,128
There's something I should explain to you.

882
00:38:17,712 --> 00:38:19,714
ANOTHER AREA FOR THE DOCENT TO EXPLAIN

883
00:38:20,339 --> 00:38:21,841
It's called "Guringul Cave."

884
00:38:23,676 --> 00:38:26,762
A LAVA CAVE FORMED
BY AN ERUPTION FROM BAENGNOKDAM

885
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:28,889
It's the highest lava cave in Korea.

886
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:30,308
700 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

887
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:32,101
Hikers are not allowed to go in.

888
00:38:32,184 --> 00:38:34,562
Only cultural heritage experts
are allowed.

889
00:38:35,229 --> 00:38:36,188
Let's go.

890
00:38:36,856 --> 00:38:38,816
ALLERGIC TO DOCENTS

891
00:38:39,442 --> 00:38:41,610
SETTING OFF AGAIN

892
00:38:44,363 --> 00:38:47,450
Let's just check out
the map of the trail here.

893
00:38:47,533 --> 00:38:49,535
HE FOUND THE TRAIL MAP

894
00:38:49,618 --> 00:38:52,913
From the Tamna Valley Bridge,
for about two and a half hours,

895
00:38:52,997 --> 00:38:54,498
it's a hard section.

896
00:38:55,249 --> 00:38:58,794
What about the other trail?
Is it easy all the way through for them?

897
00:38:58,878 --> 00:39:01,839
It's easy overall,
but there's a hard part at the end.

898
00:39:01,922 --> 00:39:04,133
Let's go. We shouldn't overthink it.

899
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:07,636
It's doable so far, Dowoon.

900
00:39:09,013 --> 00:39:11,057
TODAY'S GWANEUMSA TRAIL IS…

901
00:39:20,941 --> 00:39:23,861
SNOWY AND STEEP

902
00:39:29,909 --> 00:39:33,287
LEG FATIGUE BUILDS UP

903
00:39:40,586 --> 00:39:44,548
IT'S GOING TO BE A TOUGH HIKE

904
00:39:45,883 --> 00:39:49,637
MEANWHILE,
CAR, THE GARDEN AND CHAE-MIN

905
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:51,972
-Thanks.
-Sure.

906
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:54,809
SEONGPANAK TEAM ARRIVES
20 MINUTES AFTER THE OTHER TEAM

907
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:59,397
CHECKING OUT THE MOUNTAIN

908
00:40:00,481 --> 00:40:05,277
CURRENTLY -0.3°C,
IT IS CERTAINLY WARMER THAN LAST HIKE

909
00:40:06,612 --> 00:40:07,655
NODDING

910
00:40:07,738 --> 00:40:09,031
TAKING THEIR BACKPACKS

911
00:40:09,115 --> 00:40:10,116
We don't need crampons?

912
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:11,283
Are we putting on crampons?

913
00:40:11,367 --> 00:40:13,244
LET'S PUT THEM ON

914
00:40:17,331 --> 00:40:19,041
DENIED SINCE HE'S NOT A BUS
BUSES ONLY

915
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:20,418
I was checking if it moved.

916
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:22,086
-Does it move a lot?
-It does.

917
00:40:22,169 --> 00:40:23,963
That's a bad start for today.

918
00:40:25,756 --> 00:40:28,843
HE ENDS UP PUTTING THEM ON WHILE SITTING

919
00:40:29,718 --> 00:40:30,553
What?

920
00:40:34,390 --> 00:40:35,516
What's wrong?

921
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,642
The buckle's gone.

922
00:40:37,226 --> 00:40:39,061
THE WAIST BUCKLE'S GONE

923
00:40:39,145 --> 00:40:42,064
I guess I'm given a handicap
since the trail's easier.

924
00:40:42,815 --> 00:40:47,445
IT'S TIME TO WARM UP NOW

925
00:40:48,028 --> 00:40:49,989
People might think
we're climbing the Himalayas.

926
00:40:50,072 --> 00:40:51,490
Are you trying to stall?

927
00:40:51,574 --> 00:40:53,284
-I'm just warming up thoroughly.
-I see.

928
00:40:53,367 --> 00:40:55,411
A LOT OF FUSS WARMING UP FOR AN EASY TRAIL

929
00:40:55,494 --> 00:40:56,412
I was just wondering.

930
00:40:56,495 --> 00:40:58,330
-Let's go, Chae-min.
-Let's go.

931
00:40:58,414 --> 00:41:00,124
SEONGPANAK TEAM DEPARTS

932
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:03,878
AN ENERGETIC START UNLIKE OTHER TIMES

933
00:41:03,961 --> 00:41:06,297
-It definitely feels less cold.
-Right.

934
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:08,466
It's not bad.

935
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:10,384
THEY ARRIVE AT THE TRAIL ENTRANCE

936
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:12,970
It feels pretty different
from the other mountains.

937
00:41:13,053 --> 00:41:15,181
The signs also look expensive…

938
00:41:15,264 --> 00:41:16,849
-What do you mean?
-They look expensive.

939
00:41:16,932 --> 00:41:17,975
You know what I mean.

940
00:41:18,058 --> 00:41:22,396
Well, I'd say
the information boards are bigger.

941
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,732
Shouldn't we see our route
while we're here?

942
00:41:24,815 --> 00:41:25,649
Sounds good.

943
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:29,778
SEONGPANAK TRAIL

944
00:41:29,862 --> 00:41:33,073
THANKS TO ITS GENTLE INCLINE
AND WELL-ORGANIZED PATH

945
00:41:34,909 --> 00:41:41,874
IT'S THE MOST POPULAR TRAIL
AMONG ALL HIKERS

946
00:41:47,254 --> 00:41:50,132
EASY SECTION FOR 1 HOUR AND 40 MINUTES

947
00:41:50,216 --> 00:41:53,511
MODERATE SECTION FOR 1 HOUR AND 20 MINUTES

948
00:41:53,594 --> 00:41:57,973
HARD SECTION FOR 1 HOUR AND 30 MINUTES

949
00:41:58,891 --> 00:42:00,184
<i>It takes four and a half hours.</i>

950
00:42:00,267 --> 00:42:01,852
9.6 KM OF HIKING TO BAENGNOKDAM

951
00:42:01,936 --> 00:42:04,772
AND THEY WILL TAKE
THE SAME ROUTE TO DESCEND

952
00:42:04,855 --> 00:42:07,233
The other guys are climbing up from there.

953
00:42:07,316 --> 00:42:08,901
Ours is definitely much longer.

954
00:42:08,984 --> 00:42:11,612
-Yeah, ours is longer.
-It is.

955
00:42:11,695 --> 00:42:13,822
The incline's apparently gentle,
so let's go.

956
00:42:13,906 --> 00:42:15,074
Simple?

957
00:42:15,157 --> 00:42:16,742
-Gentle.
-I see.

958
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:21,664
Gosh, I'm so mad
that this buckle's gone.

959
00:42:22,248 --> 00:42:24,458
I should get a new K2 backpack.

960
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:25,918
Good thinking.

961
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:28,671
I'll buy new clothes
from K2 next time too.

962
00:42:29,755 --> 00:42:30,839
Good idea.

963
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:35,052
ONLY 1,000 PEOPLE A DAY CAN ENTER
SEONGPANAK WITH RESERVATIONS

964
00:42:36,011 --> 00:42:40,599
SEONGPANAK BEGINS
WITH WOODEN STEPS ON A GENTLE INCLINE

965
00:42:46,438 --> 00:42:48,065
It's a breeze so far.

966
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:51,569
If only it can be like this until the end.

967
00:42:51,652 --> 00:42:52,486
Seriously.

968
00:42:53,237 --> 00:42:56,782
If it was, it'd be nice for everyone,
including our camera operators.

969
00:42:56,865 --> 00:42:59,201
-Right.
-It'd be great for everyone.

970
00:43:00,202 --> 00:43:02,538
PRODUCER NAH SIGHS

971
00:43:02,621 --> 00:43:03,455
What?

972
00:43:04,790 --> 00:43:08,460
Overall, Producer Nah
is a pretty slow hiker.

973
00:43:08,544 --> 00:43:10,296
Should we match his pace?

974
00:43:10,963 --> 00:43:12,464
Yeah, let's go at this pace.

975
00:43:12,548 --> 00:43:14,717
I can't go faster. And Chae-min…

976
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:16,135
His strides are so long.

977
00:43:16,218 --> 00:43:17,303
He's insane.

978
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:19,722
When we hiked Seoraksan, he wasn't tired.

979
00:43:21,223 --> 00:43:23,601
If we keep pace with him, we'll be toast.

980
00:43:23,684 --> 00:43:25,769
And you know, right?

981
00:43:25,853 --> 00:43:27,855
This Seongpanak trail

982
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:29,523
is only full of the old and the weak.

983
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:31,358
This trail? Really?

984
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:32,651
-I'm "old."
-Good.

985
00:43:32,735 --> 00:43:34,194
-I'm "old."
-And I'm "weak."

986
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:35,112
"Weak."

987
00:43:35,195 --> 00:43:36,614
It's "old," "weak," and "person."

988
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:38,616
OLD NAH, WEAK CAR, CHAEMIN THE PERSON

989
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:40,034
let's take it slow.

990
00:43:40,117 --> 00:43:42,369
Still, our producer Hyun-yong
isn't here with us,

991
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:44,872
-we don't have to stop and listen to him.
-I love it.

992
00:43:44,955 --> 00:43:48,000
If he were here,
he'd be explaining what these were.

993
00:43:48,083 --> 00:43:49,918
THAT'S EXACTLY
WHAT HE'S DOING ON GWANEUMSA

994
00:43:51,754 --> 00:43:55,257
I bet Dowoon will be awfully quiet today.

995
00:43:55,341 --> 00:43:57,468
THE OLD AND WEAK
SUDDENLY WORRY ABOUT THE OTHERS

996
00:43:57,551 --> 00:43:59,053
Dowoon's not feeling well today?

997
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:00,304
It's not that.

998
00:44:00,387 --> 00:44:02,514
He just doesn't talk much while hiking.

999
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:04,725
Maybe he wants to hide his fake dialect.

1000
00:44:05,893 --> 00:44:07,394
When he's really exhausted…

1001
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:08,729
He talks in a Seoul accent.

1002
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:10,898
He's probably very confused

1003
00:44:10,981 --> 00:44:12,149
since it's all mixed up.

1004
00:44:13,567 --> 00:44:14,735
YAWNING

1005
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:18,781
GWANEUMSA TEAM HAS CLIMBED 2.5 KM

1006
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:22,493
THEY ARE STILL ON THE MODERATE SECTION

1007
00:44:29,083 --> 00:44:31,001
I'm starting to feel it.

1008
00:44:31,085 --> 00:44:32,461
-Right?
-Yeah.

1009
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:37,841
Thank goodness.

1010
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:39,176
STEPS GOING DOWN APPEAR

1011
00:44:40,386 --> 00:44:42,554
After all that climbing,
why are we going down again?

1012
00:44:42,638 --> 00:44:43,472
Right?

1013
00:44:46,433 --> 00:44:48,644
"HIKING" IS ALL ABOUT CLIMBING UP

1014
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:51,271
Damn.

1015
00:44:51,772 --> 00:44:54,149
IF THERE'S A PATH GOING DOWN

1016
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:56,276
That must be the "Stairway to Heaven."

1017
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:58,028
THERE'S ANOTHER GOING UP

1018
00:44:59,571 --> 00:45:01,615
"TO GO UP, ONE NEEDS COURAGE TO GO DOWN."
-NIETZSCHE

1019
00:45:02,116 --> 00:45:03,242
Now, it's difficult.

1020
00:45:03,325 --> 00:45:04,743
THE HARD SECTION BEGINS

1021
00:45:06,453 --> 00:45:09,623
THE STAFF'S PICK
1ST CRUX

1022
00:45:09,706 --> 00:45:11,708
These stairs are insane.

1023
00:45:13,001 --> 00:45:15,170
-Should we let them pass?
-Yeah, we should.

1024
00:45:15,754 --> 00:45:18,715
GIVING WAY FOR NO REASON

1025
00:45:19,258 --> 00:45:22,094
INTIMIDATED

1026
00:45:22,177 --> 00:45:25,848
THE END OF THE STAIRS IS BARELY VISIBLE

1027
00:45:25,931 --> 00:45:26,849
Let's go.

1028
00:45:29,852 --> 00:45:32,396
THEY START CLIMBING

1029
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,775
BARELY ENOUGH ROOM
FOR A SINGLE FOOT ON THE NARROW STEPS

1030
00:45:38,110 --> 00:45:40,612
This is dangerous. Let's be careful.

1031
00:45:42,531 --> 00:45:44,575
-Geez.
-Goodness.

1032
00:45:45,534 --> 00:45:47,786
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

1033
00:45:47,870 --> 00:45:50,914
CLIMBING USING BOTH STICKS

1034
00:45:50,998 --> 00:45:52,791
FROM DOWOON'S CAM

1035
00:45:52,875 --> 00:45:55,752
We should hold on to the ropes.
It's dangerous.

1036
00:45:59,548 --> 00:46:03,969
HOLDING ON TO THE ROPE WITH ONE HAND

1037
00:46:04,052 --> 00:46:06,096
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

1038
00:46:06,180 --> 00:46:09,141
BUT THE ROPE IS NOT TAUT ENOUGH

1039
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:13,604
<i>The sticks weren't enough,</i>
<i>so we had to hold the ropes.</i>

1040
00:46:13,687 --> 00:46:15,606
But the ropes were so loose.

1041
00:46:15,689 --> 00:46:17,441
They were limp.

1042
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:20,027
LEFT HAND, HIKING STICK
RIGHT HAND, ROPE

1043
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:22,279
HARD TO EVEN KEEP THEIR BALANCE

1044
00:46:22,362 --> 00:46:25,574
A PERSON AHEAD OF THEM
IS ALSO HOLDING ON TO THE ROPE

1045
00:46:25,657 --> 00:46:29,328
NOT ABLE TO PICK UP THE PACE

1046
00:46:29,411 --> 00:46:30,954
DEEP SIGH

1047
00:46:40,088 --> 00:46:44,134
THEY ARE HALFWAY THROUGH

1048
00:46:46,845 --> 00:46:47,804
GROANS

1049
00:46:47,888 --> 00:46:49,598
Geez.

1050
00:46:51,225 --> 00:46:52,643
Jung-won should be here.

1051
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:53,602
Right?

1052
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:56,605
THEY MUST KEEP GOING UP

1053
00:46:57,314 --> 00:47:01,735
THEY KEEP GOING WITHOUT A BREAK

1054
00:47:02,903 --> 00:47:04,071
SWAYS

1055
00:47:05,697 --> 00:47:08,450
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

1056
00:47:08,534 --> 00:47:10,160
Geez, it's even steeper here.

1057
00:47:13,747 --> 00:47:15,707
VERY STEEP

1058
00:47:21,046 --> 00:47:23,173
<i>I felt like I'd slip and fall if I rested,</i>

1059
00:47:23,257 --> 00:47:24,967
<i>so I had to keep going.</i>

1060
00:47:27,344 --> 00:47:29,596
GOING MAD

1061
00:47:38,397 --> 00:47:41,191
TARZZAN ARRIVES

1062
00:47:43,527 --> 00:47:46,446
DOWOON ARRIVES SOON AFTER

1063
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:48,532
I feel like there's less oxygen here.

1064
00:47:49,116 --> 00:47:50,367
We climbed so high.

1065
00:47:52,536 --> 00:47:54,204
SO STEEP

1066
00:47:54,913 --> 00:47:57,332
<i>Whoever said Hallasan was flat…</i>

1067
00:47:57,416 --> 00:47:58,417
Seriously…

1068
00:48:00,377 --> 00:48:02,004
It was good in the beginning.

1069
00:48:02,087 --> 00:48:04,881
I thought, "If we keep going like this,
it'll be doable."

1070
00:48:04,965 --> 00:48:08,427
But then, I slowly got angry
once the stairs started.

1071
00:48:09,803 --> 00:48:10,846
We're at 5-12 now.

1072
00:48:10,929 --> 00:48:12,180
After all that climbing?

1073
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:13,640
It's a third of the way.

1074
00:48:13,724 --> 00:48:15,726
THEY'VE COME 3 KM BUT…

1075
00:48:16,518 --> 00:48:18,812
We're just now at the welcome sign.

1076
00:48:18,895 --> 00:48:20,480
SORRY FOR THE LATE GREETINGS

1077
00:48:20,564 --> 00:48:22,065
I'm so pissed off.

1078
00:48:29,281 --> 00:48:30,157
There it is.

1079
00:48:30,949 --> 00:48:32,159
Let's go take a break.

1080
00:48:32,242 --> 00:48:33,869
THE FIRST REST AREA IS IN SIGHT

1081
00:48:33,952 --> 00:48:38,332
1 HOUR AND 17 MINUTES PASSED
THEY ARRIVE AT TAMNA VALLEY RESTROOM

1082
00:48:39,124 --> 00:48:41,960
DAZED

1083
00:48:42,544 --> 00:48:45,339
I should've borrowed
those robot legs from last night.

1084
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:48,133
-I think they'd be helpful.
-They'd really help with step.

1085
00:48:48,216 --> 00:48:49,760
THE OWNER OF THE WALKING ASSIST DEVICE

1086
00:48:49,843 --> 00:48:53,513
HYDRATING HIMSELF QUICKLY

1087
00:48:54,348 --> 00:48:56,308
God, that's nice.

1088
00:48:56,391 --> 00:48:57,726
Want some water?

1089
00:48:57,809 --> 00:48:59,394
-No, you drink it. I have some.
-Okay.

1090
00:48:59,936 --> 00:49:02,397
THEY REFUEL WITH SNACKS NEXT

1091
00:49:02,481 --> 00:49:06,109
A BITE OF THE SNACKS
HE BROUGHT FROM THE US

1092
00:49:07,611 --> 00:49:08,612
Give me the trash.

1093
00:49:08,695 --> 00:49:10,906
No, I'm going to eat it little by little.

1094
00:49:10,989 --> 00:49:13,867
THREE CAWS

1095
00:49:13,950 --> 00:49:16,536
They say a crow cawing three times
means bad luck.

1096
00:49:17,454 --> 00:49:19,164
Caw, caw, caw.

1097
00:49:19,247 --> 00:49:22,167
WILL THEY BE ABLE TO SEE
BAENGNOKDAM TODAY?

1098
00:49:22,250 --> 00:49:26,129
They say you need three generations
of luck to get such nice weather to see.

1099
00:49:26,672 --> 00:49:28,006
What do you think, Dowoon?

1100
00:49:28,090 --> 00:49:29,549
I hope my son will get to see it.

1101
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:32,803
PASSING DOWN THE RIGHT TO SEE BAENGNOKDAM

1102
00:49:32,886 --> 00:49:34,930
NODDING

1103
00:49:35,555 --> 00:49:38,100
Without Jung-won here,
I've become the grumpy one.

1104
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:39,893
DOWOON, THE GARDEN

1105
00:49:39,976 --> 00:49:40,894
Let's go.

1106
00:49:40,977 --> 00:49:43,855
But you didn't lower our morale,
so that shouldn't be a fine.

1107
00:49:43,939 --> 00:49:44,898
I agree.

1108
00:49:44,981 --> 00:49:46,483
In fact, it boosted our morale.

1109
00:49:46,566 --> 00:49:47,734
PRESIDENT TAR APPROVES

1110
00:49:47,818 --> 00:49:51,613
CAW, CAW

1111
00:49:51,697 --> 00:49:53,073
That's so annoying.

1112
00:49:53,156 --> 00:49:54,491
IT BOTHERS HIM

1113
00:49:54,574 --> 00:49:56,493
THEY LEAVE TAMNA VALLEY RESTROOM

1114
00:49:56,576 --> 00:49:58,870
Seriously, Jung-won should've come here.

1115
00:50:00,580 --> 00:50:02,666
-He missed out on this amazing scenery.
-Right.

1116
00:50:02,749 --> 00:50:04,084
What a shame.

1117
00:50:04,167 --> 00:50:07,379
MEANWHILE, THE SEONGPANAK TEAM…

1118
00:50:07,921 --> 00:50:10,257
THEY STILL LOOK LIVELY

1119
00:50:10,841 --> 00:50:12,968
THEIR FIRST INFORMATION BOARD APPEARS

1120
00:50:13,051 --> 00:50:14,428
What's the difficulty color here?

1121
00:50:14,511 --> 00:50:15,887
YOU ARE HERE
EASY

1122
00:50:15,971 --> 00:50:17,806
The red section will be hard.

1123
00:50:17,889 --> 00:50:19,307
What's with the difficult one?

1124
00:50:19,391 --> 00:50:20,726
It continues until the end.

1125
00:50:20,809 --> 00:50:22,519
-Right.
-Isn't this supposed to be easy?

1126
00:50:22,602 --> 00:50:25,647
-You came here thinking it'd be easy.
-This trail's much easier.

1127
00:50:26,440 --> 00:50:28,024
This is different from what I'd heard.

1128
00:50:28,108 --> 00:50:29,818
-Hello.
-This man's famous.

1129
00:50:29,901 --> 00:50:31,111
Hi. How old are you?

1130
00:50:31,194 --> 00:50:32,279
I'm in the seventh grade.

1131
00:50:32,362 --> 00:50:34,531
SUDDENLY TALKING
WITH A SEVENTH GRADER AND HIS MOTHER

1132
00:50:34,614 --> 00:50:37,200
Do you know who that hairy guy is?

1133
00:50:37,993 --> 00:50:40,662
Do you know me? Have you seen me before?

1134
00:50:40,746 --> 00:50:42,581
-I don't know.
-You don't?

1135
00:50:42,664 --> 00:50:44,541
That's good.
He doesn't watch YouTube much.

1136
00:50:44,624 --> 00:50:46,585
He's right. You shouldn't know me.

1137
00:50:47,169 --> 00:50:48,837
My young friend, why do you hike?

1138
00:50:48,920 --> 00:50:50,505
Because my mom made me go.

1139
00:50:52,257 --> 00:50:53,508
That's hilarious.

1140
00:50:54,468 --> 00:50:56,803
It's because of his mom.
Then, you didn't want to come?

1141
00:50:56,887 --> 00:50:58,597
THE MOTHER IS FLUSTERED

1142
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:01,057
Me too. This guy dragged me here.

1143
00:51:01,141 --> 00:51:02,893
You know he does that a lot.

1144
00:51:02,976 --> 00:51:04,102
I was totally duped.

1145
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:05,687
TWO PEOPLE WHO DRAGGED OTHERS HERE

1146
00:51:05,771 --> 00:51:07,522
Are you going up to the top?

1147
00:51:07,606 --> 00:51:09,149
Yeah. What about you?

1148
00:51:09,232 --> 00:51:10,150
I'm going too.

1149
00:51:10,233 --> 00:51:12,611
To the top? To be honest, I don't want to.

1150
00:51:12,694 --> 00:51:14,196
Dae-seong, let's go ahead.

1151
00:51:14,780 --> 00:51:15,864
Good luck on your hike.

1152
00:51:15,947 --> 00:51:17,282
Thank you. Take care.

1153
00:51:17,365 --> 00:51:19,826
FEELING THE NEGATIVE VIBE,
THEY GO ON AHEAD

1154
00:51:20,452 --> 00:51:22,996
We finally got our first answer at least.

1155
00:51:23,079 --> 00:51:25,582
-"My mom made me go."
-"My mom made me go."

1156
00:51:26,958 --> 00:51:30,837
WHY ON EARTH DO YOU HIKE?
MY MOM MADE ME GO

1157
00:51:30,921 --> 00:51:32,214
If you're a seventh grader…

1158
00:51:33,465 --> 00:51:35,342
you don't even join
your family to go eat out.

1159
00:51:35,425 --> 00:51:37,344
-True.
-But he came to Hallasan?

1160
00:51:37,427 --> 00:51:38,887
It means he's a good son.

1161
00:51:38,970 --> 00:51:40,180
Of course, he is.

1162
00:51:40,764 --> 00:51:43,141
A mom brought her son here.

1163
00:51:44,351 --> 00:51:46,019
That means

1164
00:51:46,102 --> 00:51:47,687
this trail isn't that hard.

1165
00:51:47,771 --> 00:51:49,314
-Right?
-Right.

1166
00:51:50,273 --> 00:51:54,152
ANOTHER THING THAT PROVES
THIS ISN'T A DIFFICULT TRAIL

1167
00:51:57,781 --> 00:52:01,201
A HIKER IN CASUAL CLOTHING

1168
00:52:03,995 --> 00:52:05,622
A true hiker.

1169
00:52:06,289 --> 00:52:07,916
What? Who is that?

1170
00:52:08,416 --> 00:52:10,293
I'M A HIKER

1171
00:52:10,377 --> 00:52:13,672
NEWSBOY CAP, CASHMERE COAT,
JEANS, UGG BOOTS

1172
00:52:13,755 --> 00:52:14,965
That's so stylish.

1173
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:19,928
There were many people hiking casually.

1174
00:52:20,011 --> 00:52:22,889
There was even someone
hiking in jeans and a coat.

1175
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:26,726
They just had some light crampons
on their shoes.

1176
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:30,605
I thought maybe we were
making a fuss with our outfits.

1177
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:34,359
Gosh, hiking in a coat…

1178
00:52:35,151 --> 00:52:36,820
This makes our outfits embarrassing.

1179
00:52:36,903 --> 00:52:39,906
Right. Hiking in Uggs is amazing.

1180
00:52:42,826 --> 00:52:44,286
-We're 800 m high now?
-Yeah.

1181
00:52:44,369 --> 00:52:45,829
PASSING 800 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

1182
00:52:47,372 --> 00:52:48,456
This is nice!

1183
00:52:49,457 --> 00:52:50,375
It is.

1184
00:52:50,959 --> 00:52:52,919
Doesn't it still feel
like a walking trail today?

1185
00:52:53,003 --> 00:52:53,837
Yeah.

1186
00:52:54,838 --> 00:52:57,048
Yeah, let's go like this
for another hour.

1187
00:52:57,132 --> 00:53:00,594
To be honest, I liked it.

1188
00:53:00,677 --> 00:53:04,180
In the beginning,
it felt like we went up pleasantly.

1189
00:53:04,264 --> 00:53:07,809
The area we walked was almost flat.

1190
00:53:08,435 --> 00:53:09,769
<i>It felt like a warm-up.</i>

1191
00:53:13,315 --> 00:53:15,650
<i>Thanks to the easy section,</i>

1192
00:53:16,735 --> 00:53:18,236
<i>we were able to warm up enough.</i>

1193
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:23,241
MAYBE CHAE-MIN IS TOO WARMED UP

1194
00:53:23,325 --> 00:53:24,868
WIPING SWEAT AWAY

1195
00:53:24,951 --> 00:53:26,912
It sure is hot today.

1196
00:53:27,621 --> 00:53:31,041
I might end up
taking off all my layers today.

1197
00:53:31,625 --> 00:53:32,500
It's hot.

1198
00:53:32,584 --> 00:53:34,836
UNZIPS JACKET

1199
00:53:34,920 --> 00:53:37,339
TAKING OFF GLOVES

1200
00:53:38,673 --> 00:53:41,760
ADJUSTING LAYERS

1201
00:53:42,969 --> 00:53:44,638
DRYING SWEAT

1202
00:53:46,306 --> 00:53:49,726
UNZIPS HIS INNER LAYER AS WELL

1203
00:53:51,144 --> 00:53:52,479
Hold on.

1204
00:53:52,562 --> 00:53:54,773
Could you remove the mic?
I want to take this off.

1205
00:53:54,856 --> 00:53:55,982
BREAK TIME TO ADJUST CLOTHES

1206
00:53:57,192 --> 00:53:59,277
I'm sweating so much.

1207
00:53:59,361 --> 00:54:01,488
-You'll wear only one layer?
-Yes, I'm so hot now.

1208
00:54:02,280 --> 00:54:03,907
What? Do you like undressing in public?

1209
00:54:03,990 --> 00:54:05,450
-Just one layer?
-Yes.

1210
00:54:05,533 --> 00:54:07,243
I feel so hot.
My whole back is drenched.

1211
00:54:07,327 --> 00:54:08,161
A VIGOROUS GUY

1212
00:54:08,244 --> 00:54:11,039
Gosh, he's so unpredictable.

1213
00:54:11,122 --> 00:54:12,582
You're pretty passionate.

1214
00:54:12,666 --> 00:54:14,292
Yes, that's how I usually am.

1215
00:54:15,335 --> 00:54:16,628
He's a passionate guy.

1216
00:54:16,711 --> 00:54:18,004
See the sweat here?

1217
00:54:18,088 --> 00:54:19,464
-Yeah.
-You really are sweating.

1218
00:54:19,547 --> 00:54:20,507
Yes.

1219
00:54:20,590 --> 00:54:22,008
I'm really hot right now.

1220
00:54:22,092 --> 00:54:23,593
<i>It wasn't that the trail was hard.</i>

1221
00:54:24,886 --> 00:54:27,597
It was really… It was just hot.

1222
00:54:27,681 --> 00:54:29,849
I was sweating more than the others,

1223
00:54:29,933 --> 00:54:33,561
but I think most of us
did sweat a lot too.

1224
00:54:33,645 --> 00:54:35,897
It wasn't that hot,

1225
00:54:36,564 --> 00:54:38,191
but he took his clothes off.

1226
00:54:38,984 --> 00:54:40,276
Since he's a model,

1227
00:54:40,360 --> 00:54:42,487
I thought some ad sponsor
asked him to do it.

1228
00:54:42,570 --> 00:54:43,780
WHOOSH

1229
00:54:44,322 --> 00:54:45,657
And with the sweat…

1230
00:54:45,740 --> 00:54:48,368
WIPING SWEAT AWAY

1231
00:54:50,829 --> 00:54:52,455
He keeps staring off somewhere.

1232
00:54:56,710 --> 00:54:58,461
<i>I guess it was a good idea.</i>

1233
00:54:59,045 --> 00:55:01,047
<i>It wasn't my plan.</i>

1234
00:55:01,131 --> 00:55:05,593
But I got to show off
every layer of my outfit naturally.

1235
00:55:05,677 --> 00:55:08,471
CURRENT LOCATION

1236
00:55:10,348 --> 00:55:11,808
It's a cedar forest.

1237
00:55:11,891 --> 00:55:13,852
-Cider?
-"Cedar."

1238
00:55:13,935 --> 00:55:15,061
I see.

1239
00:55:16,354 --> 00:55:20,150
A DENSE FOREST OF CEDARS
THAT ARE GREEN ALL YEAR ROUND

1240
00:55:21,693 --> 00:55:25,030
WITH A GREEN AND FLAT TRAIL INSIDE

1241
00:55:25,780 --> 00:55:27,490
I hear it emits a lot of phytoncides.

1242
00:55:27,574 --> 00:55:29,200
A FOREST TRAIL FULL OF PHYTONCIDES

1243
00:55:29,284 --> 00:55:32,078
INHALING RIGHT AWAY

1244
00:55:32,162 --> 00:55:33,872
-This is all right.
-It's nice.

1245
00:55:40,378 --> 00:55:41,671
It's beautiful here.

1246
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:43,214
Yeah, it's pretty nice here.

1247
00:55:44,132 --> 00:55:46,634
CAPTURING THE SCENERY WITH HIS FILM CAMERA

1248
00:55:51,181 --> 00:55:53,099
<i>Gosh, this mountain is really nice.</i>

1249
00:55:54,017 --> 00:55:55,810
EVEN CAR, THE GARDEN LIKES THE SCENERY

1250
00:55:55,894 --> 00:55:57,353
<i>It's so beautiful here.</i>

1251
00:56:05,070 --> 00:56:07,489
But the thing is,
this is still the easiest section.

1252
00:56:08,698 --> 00:56:10,700
-But isn't it so beautiful?
-It is.

1253
00:56:10,784 --> 00:56:12,494
It's okay so far.

1254
00:56:13,578 --> 00:56:15,246
I wonder if they're having a tough time.

1255
00:56:15,330 --> 00:56:17,082
Honestly, this trail's not bad. Right?

1256
00:56:17,165 --> 00:56:18,750
-Right.
-I feel bad.

1257
00:56:19,793 --> 00:56:21,795
WORRYING ABOUT THE GWANEUMSA TEAM

1258
00:56:24,422 --> 00:56:26,216
The trees are all cedars now.

1259
00:56:26,299 --> 00:56:28,843
THE GWANEUMSA TEAM
IS ALSO LOOKING AT THE CEDARS

1260
00:56:29,969 --> 00:56:32,013
It definitely smells different now.

1261
00:56:32,889 --> 00:56:34,182
I smell something.

1262
00:56:34,265 --> 00:56:36,976
These cedars emit a lot of phytoncides.

1263
00:56:38,561 --> 00:56:40,063
You smell it too, right?

1264
00:56:40,146 --> 00:56:42,607
I do. But it just smells like trees.

1265
00:56:43,858 --> 00:56:45,235
That was beautiful.

1266
00:56:45,318 --> 00:56:47,028
Suddenly, in the middle section…

1267
00:56:47,946 --> 00:56:49,656
The really tall ones were cedars, right?

1268
00:56:49,739 --> 00:56:51,741
The cedar forest was the most memorable.

1269
00:56:56,037 --> 00:56:58,123
I think those are animal footprints.

1270
00:56:58,206 --> 00:56:59,332
You're right.

1271
00:57:00,041 --> 00:57:02,043
-They're definitely not a human's.
-You're right.

1272
00:57:03,419 --> 00:57:04,629
Maybe a deer's?

1273
00:57:04,712 --> 00:57:05,713
Right?

1274
00:57:06,506 --> 00:57:08,091
That definitely can't be a human's.

1275
00:57:08,967 --> 00:57:10,426
DISCOVERS SOMETHING

1276
00:57:12,846 --> 00:57:14,848
I think this was a boar,
judging by the shape.

1277
00:57:14,931 --> 00:57:15,807
BOAR FOOTPRINTS?

1278
00:57:16,641 --> 00:57:19,018
FOOTPRINTS OUTSIDE THE TRAIL

1279
00:57:23,731 --> 00:57:25,066
THE SHAPES

1280
00:57:25,150 --> 00:57:28,278
AND DIRECTIONS ARE ALL DIFFERENT

1281
00:57:29,737 --> 00:57:31,364
It passed through here.

1282
00:57:32,866 --> 00:57:35,201
-Some look like a cat's.
-Right.

1283
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:42,250
Hey, someone wrote my name there.

1284
00:57:42,333 --> 00:57:43,793
-Who?
-Over here.

1285
00:57:45,628 --> 00:57:46,921
Isn't it "Jae-won"?

1286
00:57:47,922 --> 00:57:49,090
I should change it.

1287
00:57:49,632 --> 00:57:51,342
ADDS A STROKE

1288
00:57:52,760 --> 00:57:54,679
MR. LEE CHAE-WON IS SATISFIED

1289
00:57:55,305 --> 00:57:56,473
Was it written as "Dowoon"?

1290
00:57:56,556 --> 00:57:58,099
Yes, over there.

1291
00:57:58,933 --> 00:58:01,895
DOWOON

1292
00:58:01,978 --> 00:58:02,896
"Dowoon"?

1293
00:58:03,521 --> 00:58:05,273
Gosh, who was it?

1294
00:58:06,149 --> 00:58:08,234
You should've told me.

1295
00:58:08,318 --> 00:58:09,861
IT MAKES HIM HAPPY

1296
00:58:11,738 --> 00:58:12,739
This is fun.

1297
00:58:12,822 --> 00:58:14,282
It's fun seeing these.

1298
00:58:15,825 --> 00:58:17,994
I guess many people
write their names here.

1299
00:58:19,078 --> 00:58:21,706
Like a guest book, you know?

1300
00:58:21,789 --> 00:58:22,665
Right.

1301
00:58:22,749 --> 00:58:24,167
It's romantic.

1302
00:58:25,084 --> 00:58:26,461
I WAS HERE

1303
00:58:26,544 --> 00:58:28,296
LEE DONG-SEOP

1304
00:58:28,379 --> 00:58:29,839
JIN-GYU

1305
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:31,424
HYEON

1306
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:33,635
I liked that too.

1307
00:58:33,718 --> 00:58:35,637
There was snow around the trail.

1308
00:58:35,720 --> 00:58:38,681
And some people wrote
messages in the snow.

1309
00:58:38,765 --> 00:58:42,352
It was kind of like
a guest book for the trail.

1310
00:58:42,435 --> 00:58:43,895
I thought that was pretty romantic.

1311
00:58:45,980 --> 00:58:48,191
-Should we write something too?
-We should.

1312
00:58:49,400 --> 00:58:50,527
"Tarzzan was here."

1313
00:58:54,697 --> 00:58:56,032
I'll write your name big.

1314
00:59:05,792 --> 00:59:10,880
DOWOON AND TARZZAN WERE HERE

1315
00:59:11,464 --> 00:59:12,382
It's cute.

1316
00:59:16,302 --> 00:59:17,512
Put your handprint too.

1317
00:59:22,308 --> 00:59:23,893
THE TWO OF THEM WERE HAVING A NICE TIME

1318
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:26,104
If you sit, you and the message
will be in frame.

1319
00:59:26,187 --> 00:59:27,188
THE DOCENT WANTED A PHOTO

1320
00:59:27,272 --> 00:59:29,107
I need you to sit to get a good angle.

1321
00:59:29,190 --> 00:59:30,817
Good. Looks great.

1322
00:59:31,818 --> 00:59:33,820
One, two, three. Look here.

1323
00:59:38,783 --> 00:59:40,243
We shouldn't write again.

1324
00:59:41,494 --> 00:59:42,704
We learned a lesson.

1325
00:59:42,787 --> 00:59:44,205
Yeah, we did.

1326
00:59:47,000 --> 00:59:48,585
It says, "Don't come here."

1327
00:59:48,668 --> 00:59:49,919
"Don't come here."

1328
00:59:50,003 --> 00:59:51,504
DON'T COME HERE

1329
00:59:51,588 --> 00:59:54,048
A WARNING FROM SOMEONE

1330
00:59:55,216 --> 00:59:58,219
THE PATH AHEAD OF THEM

1331
00:59:58,928 --> 01:00:01,431
IS STILL A LONG WAY TO GO

1332
01:00:02,140 --> 01:00:03,766
THEY CLIMB

1333
01:00:03,850 --> 01:00:05,893
<i>Gosh, my calves are about to explode.</i>

1334
01:00:06,436 --> 01:00:07,854
<i>This part is tough too.</i>

1335
01:00:07,937 --> 01:00:10,732
AND CLIMB AGAIN

1336
01:00:11,316 --> 01:00:13,985
As soon as I saw it,
I knew it'd be really tough.

1337
01:00:14,736 --> 01:00:17,030
Honestly, it was ridiculous.

1338
01:00:20,074 --> 01:00:22,410
THE STEPS OF GWANEUMSA TRAIL
GO ON ENDLESSLY

1339
01:00:26,873 --> 01:00:29,083
<i>Seriously, it was killing me.</i>

1340
01:00:29,917 --> 01:00:32,378
<i>I thought my legs were going to give out.</i>

1341
01:00:32,462 --> 01:00:34,172
-Wait, Dowoon.
-What?

1342
01:00:34,756 --> 01:00:37,425
I have no idea how that happened.

1343
01:00:37,508 --> 01:00:39,135
I still don't remember.

1344
01:00:42,513 --> 01:00:45,016
DON'T COME HERE

1345
01:00:45,600 --> 01:00:47,644
I'm just not coming back again.

1346
01:00:48,186 --> 01:00:49,020
Hallasan?

1347
01:00:49,687 --> 01:00:50,897
I'm never coming back.

1348
01:01:48,955 --> 01:01:50,957
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
